{
  // Pathfinder - objective 5bb60cbc... description
  //
  // REMOVED 2026-08-12: this override was mis-attributed to a quest called
  // "Sales Night", which does not exist in tarkov.dev, the 1.1.0.0 capture, or
  // the wiki. The objective it targeted (5bb60cbc88a45011a8235cc5 on task
  // 5ae449c386f7744bde357697 = Pathfinder) is a type=visit objective whose
  // correct text is "Visit the Railway Exfil exit on Interchange" - confirmed
  // by BOTH game captures and tarkov.dev. The override rewrote it to "Survive
  // and extract on Interchange 7 times", corrupting accurate data; it is now
  // removed. Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Pathfinder

  // Test Drive - Part 1 - Objective description wording (now fixed upstream)
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Test_Drive_-_Part_1
  //
  // PARKED 2026-08-03: tarkov.dev now returns this exact description in BOTH
  // regular and pve (check-overrides reports it "redundant in EVERY mode"), so
  // the override is redundant. This is a wording fix, not a mode divergence, so
  // it is not in the divergence registry; commenting it out is documentation
  // only - a regression would be re-detected by the reference cross-check and
  // wiki-compare (both compare objective text against authoritative sources).
  // '5c0bd94186f7747a727f09b2': {
  //   objectives: {
  //     '5c1b765d86f77413193fa4f2': {
  //       description: 'Eliminate PMCs using an SR-25 with Hybrid 46 suppressor and Schmidt & Bender PM II 1-8x24 scope', // Was: "Eliminate PMC operatives using an SR-25 rifle with Hybrid 46 suppressor and Schmidt & Bender PM II 1-8x24 scope"
  //     },
  //   },
  // },

  // Power of Persuasion (aka "Test Drive - Part 2") - objective map/weapon/count
  //
  // MOVED to src/overrides/modes/regular/tasks.json5 2026-08-12: this is a
  // mode divergence, not a shared correction. The wiki (regular witness, last
  // edited 2026-08-09) documents "Eliminate 20 PMCs using an MP5SD on Streets of
  // Tarkov, Ground Zero or Interchange", while BOTH game captures (PvE) read
  // "Eliminate PMC operatives with an MP5SD on Woods, Ground Zero, Interchange,
  // or Customs" with count 5. tarkov.dev mirrors the PvE text into regular, so
  // the correction is regular-only. The old base entry also carried a top-level
  // `map: null` that upstream has since fixed (API serves map: null).
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Power_of_Persuasion

  // Test Drive - Part 4 - top-level map (now fixed upstream)
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Test_Drive_-_Part_4
  //
  // PARKED 2026-08-03: tarkov.dev now returns map: null in BOTH regular and pve
  // (check-overrides reports it "redundant in EVERY mode"), so the only field
  // was redundant and the entry became empty. This is an upstream catch-up, not
  // a mode divergence, so it is not in the divergence registry; commenting it
  // out is documentation only. Because this is a multi-map objective task, if
  // upstream re-populates the top-level map the reference cross-check / the
  // validateMap check will flag that the explicit `map: null` clear is needed.
  // '6574e0dedc0d635f633a5805': {
  //   map: null, // Was: { id: "5704e554d2720bac5b8b456e", name: "Shoreline" }
  // },

  // Easy-Breezy (aka "Test Drive - Part 5") - objective map/count
  //
  // MOVED to src/overrides/modes/regular/tasks.json5 2026-08-12: a mode
  // divergence. The wiki (regular witness, last edited 2026-08-05) documents
  // "Eliminate any 50 targets while using an SR-2M with suppressor and KP-SR2
  // sight on Factory", while BOTH game captures (PvE) read "...on Reserve or
  // Lighthouse" with count 30. tarkov.dev mirrors the PvE text into regular, so
  // the correction is regular-only.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Easy-Breezy

  // Forester's Duty - objective descriptions carry the count (wiki: "5 Scavs")
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Forester%27s_Duty
  // The game text omits the count (it lives in the objective data, which the
  // API already serves correctly); the override adds it to the description per
  // the wiki. The former zones/zoneNames clears were dropped 2026-08-12: the
  // API now serves empty zones and omits zoneNames, so those fields are no-ops.
  '66ab9da7eb102b9bcd08591c': {
    objectives: {
      '66ab9da7eb102b9bcd08591d': {
        description: 'Eliminate 5 Scavs on Lighthouse (In one raid)', // Was: Eliminate Scavs at the village on Lighthouse (In one raid)
      },
      '66ab9da7eb102b9bcd085922': {
        description: 'Eliminate 5 Scavs on Shoreline (In one raid)', // Was: Eliminate Scavs at the village on Shoreline (In one raid)
      },
    },
  },

  // Small Business - Part 3 - the two Woods objective descriptions
  //
  // REMOVED 2026-08-12: this override swapped the two Woods objective texts
  // ("river village" <-> "sawmill") on the theory that the game text was bugged
  // relative to the map markers. Every current source now agrees the game text
  // is correct as-is:
  //   - tarkov.dev serves obj 666733e565... = "river village" / obj 666733e743... = "sawmill"
  //   - the 2026-06-30 AND the 2026-08-12 (1.1.0.0) client captures both carry
  //     the same texts in localization.en
  //   - the wiki guide maps the FIRST Woods spot to the dilapidated village in
  //     the north (= river village), matching objective index order, and lists
  //     the sawmill as the second spot
  // The former marker-position claim could not be reproduced from current zone
  // coordinates (obj 666733e565... sits at (196, -7), well east of the known
  // sawmill anchor points around (23, 99)); re-add only with a fresh in-game
  // marker screenshot. A regression would be caught by the reference cross-check.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Small_Business_-_Part_3

  // To Great Heights! - Part 3 - Inaccurate count and description.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/To_Great_Heights!_-_Part_3
  '66058cc5bb83da7ba474aba9': {
    objectives: {
      '662ba61d3ed61b6b78187b71': {
        count: 2, // Was: 1
      },
    },
  },

